                "height": 1024,
                "alt": "A hill-sized, kneeling stone figure shelters a spring and communal hearths inside its broken rib vault. Sheep graze on its bowed head; amber lanterns mark the safe shelters below. Its makers and original purpose remain uncertain. Shepherds maintain the approach, while travellers exchange fuel, gossip and repair work for a place by the fire. The lanterns visible today are maintained lights, not an inexhaustible ancient enchantment.",
